    "narrative": "LawDog enters today\u2019s slate with **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** serving as our primary offensive catalysts. **Geraldo Perdomo** leads our daily efficiency board with a 67.55 score, buoyed by a favorable matchup against Zach Agnos (5.15 xERA) and an expected move to the #3 hole in the order, which provides the best volume-to-matchup ratio currently on the roster. While **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** faces a tougher arm in Mize (3.82 xERA), he remains a locked-in start with a 66.16 score; his elite status shields him from matchup volatility, and his presence in the #2 spot provides him with the necessary opportunities to capitalize on our league\u2019s priority on stolen bases.\n\nWe are navigating a somewhat tight daily cap, which forced a difficult decision regarding **Daulton Varsho** (57.30) and **Lawrence Butler** (57.79). Both sit on the bubble of our \u201cStrong\u201d tier, but **Lawrence Butler** gets the nod today over deeper bench options due to a 13% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage against Jos\u00e9 Soriano. **Daulton Varsho** remains in the lineup despite the tough lefty-on-lefty outlook against Rod\u00f3n, as his overall power profile provides a necessary floor. **Masyn Winn** is our most marginal start at 41.87; he survives the cut only because of his sprint speed, which is a non-negotiable metric for LawDog, even though his matchup against Ashcraft is neutralized by an elite catcher pop time that threatens his stolen base efficiency. \n\nBeyond our active starters, the bench remains mostly static today due to rest days for **Will Smith**, **Bryson Stott**, and **Taylor Ward**, while **Cal Raleigh** remains sidelined on the IL. We are keeping a close watch on the lineups for **Tyler Freeman**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Geraldo Perdomo**; as these slots are currently projected based on historical batting order trends, any drop in their lineup position will negatively impact their volume-adjusted output. With the rotation of **Yainer Diaz**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Matt Chapman**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Luis Arraez**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, and **Drew Gilbert**, we are positioned to pivot quickly if any of our current starters are scratched prior to first pitch.",
